<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chikuzen Province</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Chikuzen Province was an old province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyushu">Kyushu</a>, covering the north-western part of modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fukuoka-prefecture">Fukuoka Prefecture</a>. Its port of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hakata">Hakata</a> was for centuries Japan's main gateway for trade with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korea">Korea</a>. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-sekigahara">Battle of Sekigahara</a> in 1600 the province was given to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kuroda-nagamasa">Kuroda Nagamasa</a>, whose family ruled it as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fukuoka">Fukuoka</a> domain until 1871.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chikuzen-province.jpg" alt="Chikuzen Province" width="320" height="335" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ash_Crow · CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Provinces_of_Japan-Chikuzen.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
